# Interview Questions

**Q1. What is Inferential Statistics?**
Using sample data to make conclusions about a population.

**Q2. What is a Confidence Interval?**
A range likely to contain the true population parameter.

**Q3. When do we use a t-Test?**
When the sample size is small and the population standard deviation is unknown.

**Q4. What is a Null Hypothesis?**
A statement that assumes there is no effect or difference.

**Q5. What is a Type I Error?**
Rejecting a true null hypothesis.

**Q6. What is a Type II Error?**
Failing to reject a false null hypothesis.

**Q7. What is the difference between a one-tailed and a two-tailed test?**
A one-tailed test checks for a difference in one direction only (greater than or less than), while a two-tailed test checks for a difference in either direction.

